    "intro_html":  "Xinjiang cooking sits where China meets Central Asia, and its signature is cumin and dried chili used with a heavy hand instead of a pinch. This is a dry stir-fry, no sauce pooling in the pan, just spice clinging to seared meat with onion and cilantro. Turkey breast stands in for the usual lamb and takes the seasoning just as well. Each bowl comes to \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
